{"1-5":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":714},{"base":"G4190","lemma":"πονηρός","tr":"ponēros","gloss":"evil","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":78},{"base":"G2720","lemma":"κατευθύνω","tr":"kateuthunō","gloss":"to guide","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G0824","lemma":"ἄτοπος","tr":"atopos","gloss":"wrong","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G4160","lemma":"ποιέω","tr":"poieō","gloss":"to do","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":569},{"base":"G0575","lemma":"ἀπό","tr":"apo","gloss":"away from","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":644},{"base":"G2443","lemma":"ἵνα","tr":"hina","gloss":"in order that","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":668},{"base":"G3063","lemma":"λοιπόν","tr":"loipon","gloss":"henceforth","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G4741","lemma":"στηρίζω","tr":"stērizō","gloss":"to establish","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G4506","lemma":"ῥύομαι","tr":"rhuomai","gloss":"to rescue","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":17}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":64,"source":"both","text":"And the Lord will rescue me from every evil action and bring me safely into His heavenly kingdom. To Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.","from":3},{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":51,"source":"both","text":"The One who calls you is faithful, and He will do it.","from":3},{"book":"1CO","chapter":10,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":44,"source":"both","text":"No temptation has seized you except what is common to man. And God is faithful; He will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, He will also provide an escape, so that you can stand up under it.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":121,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":38,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will guard you from all evil; He will preserve your soul.","from":3},{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":37,"source":"both","text":"God, who has called you into fellowship with His Son Jesus Christ our Lord, is faithful.","from":3},{"book":"JHN","chapter":17,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"I am not asking that You take them out of the world, but that You keep them from the evil one.","from":3},{"book":"JUD","chapter":1,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":26,"source":"both","text":"Now to Him who is able to keep you from stumbling and to present you unblemished in His glorious presence, with great joy—","from":3},{"book":"MAT","chapter":6,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one.’","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"6-15":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":6}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G2038","lemma":"ἐργάζομαι","tr":"ergazomai","gloss":"to work","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":41},{"base":"G5100","lemma":"τις","tr":"tis","gloss":"one","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":530},{"base":"G3853","lemma":"παραγγέλλω","tr":"parangellō","gloss":"to order","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":31},{"base":"G0080","lemma":"ἀδελφός","tr":"adelphos","gloss":"brother","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":343},{"base":"G0814","lemma":"ἀτάκτως","tr":"ataktōs","gloss":"idly","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G3361","lemma":"μή","tr":"mē","gloss":"not","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":1068},{"base":"G3401","lemma":"μιμέομαι","tr":"mimeomai","gloss":"to imitate","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"G0235","lemma":"ἀλλά","tr":"alla","gloss":"but","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":638},{"base":"G2068","lemma":"ἐσθίω","tr":"esthiō","gloss":"to eat","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":65},{"base":"G2443","lemma":"ἵνα","tr":"hina","gloss":"in order that","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GAL","chapter":6,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":29,"source":"openbible","text":"Let us not grow weary in well-doing, for in due time we will reap a harvest if we do not give up.","from":13},{"book":"GAL","chapter":6,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":29,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore, as we have opportunity, let us do good to everyone, and especially to the family of faith.","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":26,"source":"both","text":"By the sweat of your brow you will eat your bread, until you return to the ground— because out of it were you taken. For dust you are, and to dust you shall return.”","from":10},{"book":"PRO","chapter":20,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"The slacker does not plow in season; at harvest time he looks, but nothing is there.","from":10},{"book":"1TH","chapter":4,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"and to aspire to live quietly, to attend to your own matters, and to work with your own hands, as we instructed you.","from":10},{"book":"PRO","chapter":13,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"The slacker craves yet has nothing, but the soul of the diligent is fully satisfied.","from":10},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"The craving of the slacker kills him because his hands refuse to work.","from":10},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Consider Him who endured such hostility from sinners, so that you will not grow weary and lose heart.","from":13}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"16-18":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[{"id":"athens-g0116","name":"Athens","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"thessalonica-g2332","name":"Thessalonica","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"words":[{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":714},{"base":"G1515","lemma":"εἰρήνη","tr":"eirēnē","gloss":"peace","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":92},{"base":"G3326","lemma":"μετά","tr":"meta","gloss":"with","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":465},{"base":"G0783","lemma":"ἀσπασμός","tr":"aspasmos","gloss":"salutation","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G5158","lemma":"τρόπος","tr":"tropos","gloss":"way","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G1992","lemma":"ἐπιστολή","tr":"epistolē","gloss":"epistle","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"G4592","lemma":"σημεῖον","tr":"sēmeion","gloss":"sign","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":75},{"base":"G5485","lemma":"χάρις","tr":"charis","gloss":"grace","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":155},{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":158},{"base":"G5495","lemma":"χείρ","tr":"cheir","gloss":"hand","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":175}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":29,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":33,"source":"both","text":"The LORD gives His people strength; the LORD blesses His people with peace.","from":16},{"book":"JHN","chapter":16,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"I have told you these things so that in Me you may have peace. In the world you will have tribulation. But take courage; I have overcome the world!”","from":16},{"book":"MAT","chapter":1,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"“Behold, the virgin will be with child and will give birth to a son, and they will call Him Immanuel” (which means, “God with us”).","from":16},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Peace I leave with you; My peace I give to you. I do not give to you as the world gives. Do not let your hearts be troubled; do not be afraid.","from":16},{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"The God of peace be with all of you. Amen.","from":16},{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.","from":16},{"book":"JDG","chapter":6,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"So Gideon built an altar to the LORD there and called it The LORD Is Peace. To this day it stands in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.","from":16},{"book":"LUK","chapter":2,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"“Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace to men on whom His favor rests!”","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]}}